{"gene1":{"symbol":"PAX1","uniprot":"P15863","is_essential":false,"chromosome":{"chromosome":"20","start":"21705659","end":"21718481","strand":"1"},"description":{"name":"Paired box protein Pax-1","function":"This protein is a transcriptional activator. It may play a role in the formation of segmented structures of the embryo. May play an important role in the normal development of the vertebral column (By similarity)"},"known_drugs":[]},"gene2":{"symbol":"PAX5","uniprot":"Q02548","is_essential":false,"chromosome":{"chromosome":"9","start":"36833269","end":"37034268","strand":"-1"},"description":{"name":"Paired box protein Pax-5","function":"Transcription factor that plays an essential role in commitment of lymphoid progenitors to the B-lymphocyte lineage (PubMed:10811620, PubMed:27181361). Fulfills a dual role by repressing B-lineage inappropriate genes and simultaneously activating B-lineage-specific genes (PubMed:10811620, PubMed:27181361). In turn, regulates cell adhesion and migration, induces V(H)-to-D(H)J(H) recombination, facilitates pre-B-cell receptor signaling and promotes development to the mature B-cell stage (PubMed:32612238). Repression of the cohesin-release factor WAPL causes global changes of the chromosomal architecture in pro-B cells to facilitate the generation of a diverse antibody repertoire (PubMed:32612238)"},"known_drugs":[]},"pair":{"wgd":false,"family_size":51,"closest":false,"same_chr":false,"interact_bioplex":false,"n_shared_ppi":0,"ppi_network":{"shared":[],"unique_gene1":[{"id":"4222","symbol":"MEOX1","display":"MEOX1 (4222)"},{"id":"4223","symbol":"MEOX2","display":"MEOX2 (4223)"},{"id":"9493","symbol":"KIF23","display":"KIF23 (9493)"}],"unique_gene2":[{"id":"10055","symbol":"SAE1","display":"SAE1 (10055)"},{"id":"1018","symbol":"CDK3","display":"CDK3 (1018)"},{"id":"1027","symbol":"CDKN1B","display":"CDKN1B (1027)"},{"id":"10286","symbol":null,"display":"10286"},{"id":"11011","symbol":"TLK2","display":"TLK2 (11011)"},{"id":"113251",